// EXPRESSIVENESS GAP, NOT A SOUNDNESS GAP -- the SAFE-DIRECTION failure,
// unlike every other file in this directory (this file is a plain
// bad_*, expected to reject, and it does). Written to test: is there a
// row a generic can require of its TYPE PARAMETER, rather than of a
// require of its TYPE PARAMETER, rather than of a value? The natural
// extension of `sicut IDENT` (Sec 4.2 -- defined over a named VALUE
// parameter of function type: "names one of the callee's parameters")
// would be `poscit sicut T` for a generic's own type parameter's
// dictionary. Sec 8.6's grammar does not distinguish this from the
// value form at parse time -- `RowItem ::= Path | 'sicut' IDENT` accepts
// any IDENT, including a GenericParam's name -- so this is not a syntax
// error. It has no defined MEANING, though: GenericParam ::= IDENT
// [':' Type] carries no row, and Sec 4.2's substitution is resolved by
// finding a matching entry in `enclosing.params` (a VALUE parameter
// list) -- T is not in it, by construction, being a type parameter.
//
// What actually happens here is not "the checker understood and
// rejected sicut-on-a-type-parameter." `sicut T` silently contributes
// NOTHING to total_polimorfico's declared_atoms() (only ('atom', _)
// entries count, and this is a ('sicut', 'T') entry) -- exactly Sec
// 4.2's own description of the ORIGINAL closure-capture bug, one level
// up: "the prototype produced `requires [sicut f]` inside a function
// having no `f`." Here it is `poscit sicut T` inside a function whose
// only `T` is a type, not a value -- there is nothing for the name to
// attach to, again by construction and not by an oversight a smarter
// parser would close.
//
// Unlike the original bug, this fails CLOSED, not open: the file is
// REJECTED, because the dictionary-call mechanism (see
// ok_generic_dictionary_declared.exsc) still independently computes
// a.combine(b)'s real cost from Summable's declared ceiling ({alloc}),
// and an empty declared_atoms() cannot cover it. A generic wanting to
// say "whatever my dictionary needs" has no expressible way to do so
// today; it can only fall back to declaring the trait's own ceiling by
// hand, which is what every OTHER file in this directory does. Expect
// under the checker as implemented: reject, EXS-E0421 -- for the
// "undeclared row" reason, not for any reason naming `sicut T` itself.

interfacies Summable {
    functio combine(self, other: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc
}

functio usa_rete(x: f32) -> f32 poscit rete {
    redde x;
}

interfacies Summable in Right poscit alloc, rete {
    functio combine(self, other: f32) -> f32 {
        redde usa_rete(other);
    }
}

publica functio total_polimorfico<T: Summable>(a: T, b: f32) -> f32 poscit sicut T {
    redde a.combine(b);
}
